```dart
/// The warm-switch resumed-context cache (gh-1734): ...
library;

import '../session_tree.dart';

/// One cached context entry keyed by the session file's stat fingerprint.
final class _Entry {
 _Entry({required this.sizeBytes, required this.mtimeMs, required this.context});
 final int sizeBytes;
 final int mtimeMs;
 final SessionContext context;
}

final class ResumedContextCache {
 ResumedContextCache({int capacity = 4}) : capacity = capacity < 1 ? 1 : capacity;
 final int capacity;
 final _entries = <String, _Entry>{};

 int get length => _entries.length;

 SessionContext? match(String path, {required int sizeBytes, required int mtimeMs}) {
  final entry = _entries[path];
  if (entry == null) return null;
  if (entry.sizeBytes != sizeBytes || entry.mtimeMs != mtimeMs) {
    _entries.remove(path);
    return null;
  }
  // LRU refresh: re-insert at the most-recent position.
  _entries.remove(path);
  _entries[path] = entry;
  return SessionContext(
    messages: List.of(entry.context.messages),
    thinkingLevel: entry.context.thinkingLevel,
    model: entry.context.model,
    activeToolNames: entry.context.activeToolNames == null ? null : List.of(entry.context.activeToolNames!),
  );
 }

 void remember(String path, {required int sizeBytes, required int mtimeMs, required SessionContext context}) {
  if (_entries.containsKey(path)) _entries.remove(path);
  _entries[path] = _Entry(sizeBytes: sizeBytes, mtimeMs: mtimeMs, context: context);
  while (_entries.length > capacity) {
    _entries.remove(_entries.keys.first);
  }

 void clear() => _entries.clear();
}
``

Is `SessionContext` mutable? No — final fields. `messages` is a List — copied on hand-out; the STORED context keeps the built list which nobody else holds (the caller gets the built context passed in... wait — in `_loadSessionInner`, when I `remember(path, context: built)`, the built context's message list could ALSO be referenced by `_agent.state.messages` (same instance!) — the agent mutates ITS list — which IS the same list! `resetLoadedUsageAnchors(messages)` creates a NEW list, so `_agent.state.messages` is a fresh list; the built list is only held by the cache. But `context.messages` — the `SessionContext` I built — `messages: await _projectMessages(...)` — one list instance. `_agent.state.messages = resetLoadedUsageAnchors(messages)` — where messages = context.messages — resetLoadedUsageAnchors returns a new list. So no aliasing with the agent state. 

But careful: `localTrimValve` in `_capResumedContext` may set `_agent.state.messages = trimmed.messages` — again new. OK.

Also the FIRST load of a session stores the context; the SECOND load (cache hit) hands a copy to resetLoadedUsageAnchors — new list. Good.

One more aliasing check: on the hit path I return a NEW SessionContext with copied list — `messages = resetLoadedUsageAnchors(copy)` — the copy is consumed. The ORIGINAL cached list untouched. 

